data)) {\n        // Don't strip the national prefix.\n        return {\n          nationalNumber: number\n        };\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return {\n    nationalNumber: nationalNumber\x2C\n    carrierCode: carrierCode\n  };\n}\n\n// In some countries\x2C the same digit could be a national prefix\n// or a leading digit of a valid phone number.\n// For example\x2C in Russia\x2C national prefix is `8`\x2C\n// and also `800 555 35 35` is a valid number\n// in which `8` is not a national prefix\x2C but the first digit\n// of a national (significant) number.\n// Same's with Belarus:\n// `82004910060` is a valid national (significant) number\x2C\n// but `2004910060` is not.\n// To support such cases (to prevent the code from always stripping\n// national prefix)\x2C a condition is imposed: a national prefix\n// is not extracted when the original number is "viable" and the\n// resultant number is not\x2C a "viable" national number being the one\n// that matches `national_number_pattern`.\nfunction shouldHaveExtractedNationalPrefix(nationalNumberBefore\x2C nationalNumberAfter\x2C metadata) {\n  // The equivalent in Google's code is:\n  // https://github.com/google/libphonenumber/blob/e326fa1fc4283bb05eb35cb3c15c18f98a31af33/java/libphonenumber/src/com/google/i18n/phonenumbers/PhoneNumberUtil.java#L2969-L3004\n  if ((0\x2C _matchesEntirely["default"])(nationalNumberBefore\x2C metadata.nationalNumberPattern()) && !(0\x2C _matchesEntirely["default"])(nationalNumberAfter\x2C metadata.nationalNumberPattern())) {\n    return false;\n  }\n  // This "is possible" national number (length) check has been commented out\n  // because it's superceded by the (effectively) same check done in the\n  // `extractNationalNumber()` function after it calls `shouldHaveExtractedNationalPrefix()`.\n  // In other words\x2C why run the same check twice if it could only be run once.\n  // // Check the national (significant) number length after extracting national prefix and carrier code.\n  // // F